2540 * ōccha 'small, thin, mean'. Pk. uccha - 'low, mean'; Dm. ū́čha , ū́ča 'little'; Kal. učī́k 'light (of weight)'; Phal. účo 'a little'; S. ocho 'paltry, mean', L. (Shahpur) ochā , awāṇ. hochā ; P. ochā 'light, vain, absurd'; WPah. bhal. hoccho 'mean,
low'; Ku. occho , wac° 'mean, contemptible, arrogant';
Or. ocha 'small, mean, exhausted'; Bhoj. ōch 'mean';
H. ochā 'empty, small, silly'; OG. uchaü 'less', G. ochũ 'deficient, inferior'; M. os 'desolate, depopulated', osā m. 'empty space in a cornfield'; — M. otsā light, mean,
deficient' ← H. or G. Addenda: * ōccha- [~ * hōccha - Add²; cf. WPah.kṭg. ókkhɔ 'small' ~ * hōkkha - Add²]: S.kcch. ochū̃ keṇū 'to
lessen'.
